  "description": "PIVWAU crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2. Reported CIF formula moiety: C56 H95 Dy3 N8 O15 2+,C54 H87 Dy3 N10 O19,6(C1 H4 O1),2(N1 O3 1-). From the CIF bond table, Dy3 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy1 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.512-3.540 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.50-97.33°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C54H95Dy3N10O23. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 3 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
